 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "Start anywhere, a0. Seriality gives a successor a1 ≠ a0 (irreflexivity forbids a0 → a0).",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "e01",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Keep going: a1 → a2 and a2 → a3. Transitivity already forces a0 → a2, a0 → a3, a1 → a3, so no element can point back to an earlier one without trouble.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "e12",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "e23",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "a3 needs a successor too. There are only 4 elements and a3 → a3 is forbidden, so it must point back to one already visited, say a1.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "e31",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    },
    {
     "id": "note",
     "set": {
      "text": "pigeonhole: the chain must revisit an element",
      "tone": "warning"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Transitivity along the loop: a1 → a3 (from a1 → a2 → a3) and a3 → a1 give a1 → a1. Irreflexivity is violated.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "e13",
     "set": {
